# Canonical Praxion baseline principles.yaml — the eight dimensions of
# beautiful code as advisory project principles.
#
# Single source of truth for the managed-project seed. /onboard-project
# §Phase 2 (and /new-project via its chain) installs this as
# `.ai-state/principles.yaml` when none exists — never overwriting an
# existing one. This is what makes the dimensions an ACTIVE gate in a
# managed project's pipeline: the implementation-planner threads matching
# principles into step acceptance criteria (Phase 1b) and the verifier
# gates them in Phase 4.5. All rows ship `advisory` (WARN, never FAIL).
# Schema: skills/software-planning/references/project-principles.md
# Canon and review checks: skills/beautiful-code/SKILL.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file is YOURS, project: edit statements, narrow scopes to your layout,
# promote a row to `severity: blocking` once the team commits to it, or
# delete rows that do not apply. Praxion seeds it; it never overwrites it.
version: 1
principles:
  - id: beauty-storytelling
    statement: Changed files read top-down by decreasing abstraction, comments say only what the code cannot (why, invariants, cross-file obligations), and the change lands as named revertible steps
    severity: advisory
    scope: "*"
    rationale: Code is written for the human who reads it next; narrative order and why-comments are the cheapest comprehension levers (coding-style § Reading Order and Narrative)
  - id: beauty-simplicity
    statement: Every added line, parameter, flag, and abstraction serves a requirement that exists today, and no new module's interface merely mirrors its implementation
    severity: advisory
    scope: "*"
    rationale: Simplicity First made checkable — the YAGNI gate plus the deep-module test; simple is un-braided, not familiar
  - id: beauty-clarity-of-intent
    statement: Behavior and side effects are predictable from names and signatures alone, using full words or established domain notation
    severity: advisory
    scope: ["**/*.py", "**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.js", "**/*.jsx", "**/*.go", "**/*.rs", "**/*.java", "**/*.kt", "**/*.rb", "**/*.swift", "**/*.c", "**/*.cpp", "**/*.sh"]
    rationale: Intention-revealing names are empirically faster to comprehend; a reader should not need the body to know the contract (coding-style § Naming)
  - id: beauty-expressiveness
    statement: Each construct states its intent directly — declarative where it removes mental simulation, explicit where ordering or effects need visibility — and nothing requires decoding rather than reading
    severity: advisory
    scope: ["**/*.py", "**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.js", "**/*.jsx", "**/*.go", "**/*.rs", "**/*.java", "**/*.kt", "**/*.rb", "**/*.swift", "**/*.c", "**/*.cpp", "**/*.sh"]
    rationale: Notation is a tool of thought; density that must be decoded is cleverness, not expressiveness (coding-style § Expressive Constructs)
  - id: beauty-purity
    statement: New logic separates gather, compute, and use — pure core, effects at owned edges — with every input visible in the signature and core logic testable without mocks
    severity: advisory
    scope: ["**/*.py", "**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.js", "**/*.jsx", "**/*.go", "**/*.rs", "**/*.java", "**/*.kt", "**/*.rb", "**/*.swift", "**/*.c", "**/*.cpp"]
    rationale: Most defects are unconsidered states; explicit state and isolated effects shrink the state space (coding-style § Side-Effect Discipline)
  - id: beauty-sustainability
    statement: Changes to untested code are preceded by characterization tests, incomplete understanding is visibly recorded (ledger, ADR, or owned TODO), and cleanup stays within the files the change already touches
    severity: advisory
    scope: "*"
    rationale: Debt is incomplete understanding made visible, never sanctioned sloppiness; boy-scouting is bounded by Stay Surgical
  - id: beauty-durability
    statement: Observable behavior of consumed surfaces survives the change unchanged, or the change carries an explicit deprecation or versioning path; boundaries reject malformed input contractually
    severity: advisory
    scope: "*"
    rationale: All observable behavior is somebody's contract (Hyrum's Law); silent tolerance calcifies divergence (coding-style § Compatibility and Deprecation)
  - id: beauty-creativity
    statement: Non-obvious solutions document the domain premise they exploit, name their concrete payoff, and spend novelty only where the problem is genuinely novel; language-trick cleverness stays out of production paths
    severity: advisory
    scope: "*"
    rationale: Creativity is licensed at the design level (insight, reframing) and banned at the line level (tricks); an undocumented premise is the failure mode (beautiful-code § Creativity)
